WEBVTT

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.870
It's so hot...

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.460
I can't take it anymore!

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.670
Can you use magic to
make cold water for me?

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:27.710
Sure. Why're you asking?

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.720
I want to cool off by soaking
my feet in some cold water.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:32.970
What?! I mean, sure, but...

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.600
I know, I know! It's improper
for a lady to show her bare feet!

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.020
Just make sure nobody
sees you like that, okay?

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.150
Thanks!

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.320
Oh, could you put some ice in there, too?

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:50.070
What?! You know you're
asking for the impossible, right?!

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.990
The only people who can make ice are ice
mages, and there aren't very many of <i>them</i>!

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.660
Oh, is that right?

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:57.950
That's annoying.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.630
This is just what I needed.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:08.880
Come in!

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.380
Sei, may I--

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.440
Good afternoon, Commander Hawke!

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.490
What fine weather we're having today.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:56.660
My apologies.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.370
Stop, you're gonna make <i>me </i>embarrassed!

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:02.080
So, uh, what is it you needed of me?

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.500
Ah, yes. I heard you were taking
a day away from work tomorrow,

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.710
and was wondering if you'd like
to come into town with me.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.960
That is, if you don't already have plans.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.590
You're going into town?!

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:15.380
I take it you don't have any plans, then?

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:19.340
You told me you sometimes
spend your days off hard at work,

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:22.350
so I thought a little excursion might give
you an opportunity to relax instead.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.810
Thank you for thinking of me.
I would love to come with you.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.440
Then I shall come to meet
you tomorrow morning.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.310
Sounds great!

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:34.230
In that moment,
I had completely forgotten

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:39.070
that I'd be going with the Ice Knight,
who seemed to melt in my presence.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.790
You should be able to see
the town now, Sei.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:58.210
Capital

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.480
Th-Thank you.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.230
Down yonder is the marketplace.
Shall we head there together?

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.270
Yes, let's.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.160
Huh?

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:27.660
Wait, is he just gonna keep holding it?!

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.400
Careful, now.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:54.440
Th-Thank you.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.070
Try to stay close to me if you can.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:58.240
O-Of course.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.160
How are you doing?

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.040
F-Fine, why do you ask?

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.870
Are you hungry at all?

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:13.420
Oh, sure. I suppose I'm a little hungry.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:17.130
Very well. Why don't we stop for a
bite at one of the food stands here?

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.180
Here you are.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.890
Th-Thank you again.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:34.520
What's the matter?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:39.230
Oh, nothing. I just expected something
different. You seem... used to all this.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.740
Johan and I came here often in the past.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:46.120
You did? I didn't know members of the
upper class would go into town that often.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.910
They don't. We would sneak out.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:50.660
Don't tell anyone.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:53.960
Of course.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:59.130
Oh, right, how much was this?

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.460
You needn't worry about that.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:03.130
Wait, but...

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.680
Thank you for the treat, then.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.890
It's delicious!

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.440
What's wrong?

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.900
Oh, uh...

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.490
Is it not to your liking?

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:24.280
No, it's quite good.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.910
I just wish it were a little
bit colder, that's all.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.090
Was that just...

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:50.010
Thank you so much! It's even better now.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.600
I'm glad to be of service.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:02.320
There are a menagerie
of shopfronts down that way.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.240
Would you mind if we went there next?

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.320
No, not at all!

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.770
Forgive me, but is it all right
if I take care of this business?

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.020
Of course, go right ahead.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.570
This is incredible...

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.820
And sure enough,

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.570
the price is <i>just </i>as incredible.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.910
Sei! Did you find something you fancy?

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:57.370
No, it's all right.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:01.290
This is way out of my budget, so I'll
have to come back for it another time.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.180
Sei?

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:20.850
You've been asleep for a while.
You must have been quite exhausted.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:26.030
I-I hope I didn't drool or anything!

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.320
D-Don't laugh at me!

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.950
Thank you so much for the outing today.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:38.040
No, thank <i>you</i>. I had a lovely time.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.920
Same here! It was so much fun.

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:44.380
Have a good night.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:46.460
Sei.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:48.630
Yes?

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:51.760
Here.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.600
For me?

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.310
I hope this will be to your liking.

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:03.980
What--

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:06.820
Please wait until you return
to your room to open it!

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.820
Huh? Wait!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:09.240
Commander Hawke...

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:26.380
How'd it go yesterday?

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:27.960
We had a lovely time.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:32.630
Here's the report you requested.
If you'll excuse me, then.

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:34.510
Where'd you guys go?

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:35.680
Why do you ask?

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.060
I just want to know.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.640
We went into town.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:39.730
Then what?

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:44.770
We ate food from a stand, went around to a
few shops, then went home around sunset.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:46.230
It was nothing special.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.610
That's surprisingly wholesome.

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:51.740
Nevertheless, I'm glad you
two had fun on your date.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.030
What's the matter?

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.200
What do you mean, <i>date</i>?

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.200
We just went into town, that's all.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:04.040
You and Al went into town together,
had some food, and went shopping, yeah?

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.580
That's right.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.550
And that's not a date?

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:13.340
No, it can't be! Commander Hawke had
things to do in town, so I came along!

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.760
But he invited you to come
with him, didn't he?

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.100
Well, yes, but still!

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:21.390
He only invited me to come with him
because he wanted company, that's all!

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:22.980
Even if that were the case,

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:26.810
he wouldn't invite a woman he wasn't
romantically interested in, would he?

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:30.780
<i>R-Romantically</i>? I...

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:32.900
Was he cruel to you, then?

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.030
No, of course not!

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:37.830
He even helped me get down from
the carriage when we got there.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:42.000
I just thought that was something
the upper class did for women!

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.460
I mean, yeah.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:44.790
See?

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:47.210
He held my hand when we
were walking through town,

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.710
and he bought me a small
souvenir on our way home.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:50.710
He did?

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:59.560
It's the same beautiful hair ornament I
saw in town, but the stones are different.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:00.680
How very interesting.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:08.270
Just so you know, it's common for men
to help women down from carriages.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:09.480
Okay.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:15.110
But Al wouldn't give you a hair
ornament as a mere souvenir.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:23.660
Then... is it really appropriate
for me to accept a gift like this?

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.750
I'd say if you like it, then keep it.

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:42.260
What a remarkable ornament!

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.020
Was it a gift from someone?

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:45.810
Huh? How'd you know?

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:49.100
It's a bit too luxurious for everyday use.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.360
That's how I knew it had
to be a gift of sorts.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:55.490
And let me guess...
It's a gift from Commander Hawke, yes?

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:57.030
H-H-How'd you know?!

00:11:57.030 --> 00:12:00.240
Why, it was obvious!

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.370
The precious stones set into the
ornament are the same color as his eyes.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.460
You sure have an eye for detail.

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:09.790
Not at all. It's a fairly common custom.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:15.090
Men often give women they fancy
items that match the color of their eyes.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:21.550
B-But Commander Hawke couldn't possibly--

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.220
My goodness, Sei, you're so very
cute when you blush like that!

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:27.230
I-I'm just not used to
this kind of attention!

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.480
It's enchanted?

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:38.990
Yeah. Your hairpin's reacting
to your own magic power.

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:41.450
What kind of enchantment is on it?

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:43.580
Not sure.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.580
We'd need someone who knows appraisal
magic, and there's no one like that here.

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:49.250
That's too bad. It sounds interesting.

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:50.250
Huh?

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.840
I see. So that hair accessory
of yours is enchanted, too.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:59.260
He totally knew this
whole time, didn't he?

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:00.970
Want to give it a try?

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:02.010
What?

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:03.720
You've taken an interest in it, yes?

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:07.140
Sure, but it can't be that easy, can it?

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.890
Your first problem's
gonna be material cost.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:12.400
That, and very few people have the
know-how or ability to enchant items.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:17.440
Let me guess, an enchanted item
costs way more than a regular one...

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.490
Substantially more, yeah.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:25.370
I can get you a teacher.
If you want, of course.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:38.460
So <i>this </i>is the Royal Magi Assembly...

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:40.050
Thank you for your patience.

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:43.430
Allow me to explain
the theory of enchantment.

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:45.600
By all means, please.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.680
First, one selects a focus.

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:51.350
Then, they channel magic into it while
thinking upon the desired enchantment.

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:55.810
The effects possible are dependent
on the caster's elemental affinity,

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:58.860
as well as the quality
of the focus selected.

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:01.320
What type of effect
would you like to imbue?

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:02.910
Let me think...

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:12.410
Is it possible to completely
resist one type of magic?

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.540
Full resistance? That might be difficult.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.050
However, if you're able
to cast holy affinity magic,

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:20.630
then you could enchant it with a slight
mitigation to a particular affinity.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.260
Holy affinity magic...

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:26.300
Sure, let's do that.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:30.770
Very well. This focus would be
well-suited for that enchantment.

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:37.440
If I'm going to the
trouble of enchanting it,

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:40.820
I might as well have it mitigate
damage for <i>all </i>affinities...

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:42.610
I just gotta focus on that.

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.620
I-I broke it!

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:49.450
What?!

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:50.700
You sure did.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:53.750
But that's impossible!

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:59.090
You tried to imbue it with damage
mitigation for one affinity, yes?

00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:00.090
H-Huh?

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:05.340
That's <i>all </i>you were
trying to imbue it with?

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:07.260
Oh, uh, no...

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:09.180
What did you try, then?

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:13.640
I figured, why mitigate against <i>one </i>type
when you could do it for <i>all </i>of them...

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:16.520
This focus isn't nearly
strong enough for that.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:21.190
Are you sure?

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:22.280
Yes.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:31.910
It didn't break this time!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:38.130
Appraise.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:44.130
A successful enchantment.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.550
Next.

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:54.890
Enchant this to mitigate poison damage.

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:56.190
O-Okay.

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:00.020
Here you are.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:01.320
Appraise.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:04.780
Good. Next, try resist poison damage.

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:05.940
O-Okay!

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.110
Next, resistance against
paralysis and confusion.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.410
O-Okay!

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:13.990
Next, resist petrify and
mitigate all magic damage.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.200
Okay!

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:18.670
Last one.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:22.130
I-It's pretty big...

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:25.880
Enchant this with resist all status
ailments, resist physical damage,

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.470
and resist magic damage.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:37.640
I don't think I can make it resist both
physical <i>and </i>magic damage

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:39.230
at the same time.

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:42.650
But I could have it increase physical
and magical defense instead.

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:44.570
Very well. Give it a go.

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:55.200
My hands have never felt
<i>this </i>hot while casting before...

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.250
Done!

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:08.300
Appraise.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:11.720
Enchantment successful.

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:16.060
Wh-What?

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:18.930
Don't mind them.
You've done good work today.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:20.230
Take this as compensation.

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:28.650
Wait... are you sure?

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:31.990
Absolutely.
The work you've done is worth it.

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:34.370
If you say so.

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:35.660
Thank you.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.340
You called for me, Ser?

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:50.470
Come take a seat.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:58.470
There's something we'd like
to propose to you, Sei.

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:04.940
The Assembly took into possession
the foci you enchanted previously.

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:08.690
However, word of those foci seems to have
made its way to the Knightly Orders.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:12.360
So now, the Orders have asked the Assembly
to create those enchantments for them.

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.950
Unfortunately, our mages
are unable to produce

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:18.290
many of the requested enchantments.

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:20.620
The very same enchantments you
were able to successfully imbue.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:29.380
And they wouldn't believe our most
powerful mages had help from an outsider.

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:30.920
Uh-huh...

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:35.470
I hate to impose upon you like this, but
would you mind assisting us once more?

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.140
Sure, I don't mind.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:44.020
Just this once, all right?
And be sure to pay her.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:45.150
You have my gratitude.

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:03.370
We start work early most days.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.170
Is it always like this for
the Royal Magi Assembly?

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.130
Not at all.

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:10.630
We were told to ensure the request was
fulfilled before their next expedition.

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:13.300
Unfortunately,
that's happening quite soon.

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:16.590
Guess crunch exists over here, too...

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:20.140
Which Order made the request? The Third?

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:22.430
No, the First.

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:24.730
I ordered the Assembly not to
mention your enchantments,

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:26.850
but <i>someone's </i>tongue must have slipped.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:36.030
Because of that, we now need to ask for
your assistance. My sincerest apologies.

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:37.990
Oh, no, it's okay.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:40.740
Where are you going?

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:44.000
Oh, uh, I just wanted to get some potions.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.000
You stay seated.

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:48.790
It's okay, they're for me, anyway.

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:51.420
There's no need for you
to carry such heavy items.

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:09.020
Sei? Sei?

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:13.780
Are you all right?

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:15.030
Oh, yes.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:21.030
You've already done this much?

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:24.870
I should finish all of my work tomorrow.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:25.950
Is that so?

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:30.500
Appraise.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.090
Appraise.

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:35.590
Appraise.

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:42.300
Brilliantly executed. I expected no less.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.340
He's smiling!

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:46.020
It's a miracle!

00:20:51.690 --> 00:20:53.650
Gone already?

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:55.360
Thank you again for your help.

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:58.700
If you don't mind me asking,
how would you like to be compensated?

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:02.120
I have an idea.

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:38.710
Okay!

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:47.100
Yes?

00:22:47.100 --> 00:22:49.930
Pardon the intrusion, Ser Commander,
but you have a visitor.

00:22:53.940 --> 00:22:55.060
Sei!

00:22:55.980 --> 00:22:57.480
What brings you here?

00:22:57.480 --> 00:23:02.030
I made some desserts.
I thought you might like to try some.

00:23:02.030 --> 00:23:04.150
You did? That's very kind of you.

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:07.780
W-Well, I wouldn't want to interrupt
your work, so I'll see you later!

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:08.830
What's this?

00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:12.790
O-Oh, uh...

00:23:12.790 --> 00:23:15.460
It's to thank you for the hair ornament.

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:18.750
I had an opportunity to learn enchantment
at the Royal Magi Assembly,

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:23.170
and they referred me to a
craftsman they're partnered with.

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:26.840
The gem is enchanted to mitigate
magic damage of all affinities,

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:29.720
so I hope it'll come in handy when
you go out on your next expediti--

00:23:34.690 --> 00:23:37.230
That was the last thing I remember.

00:23:37.230 --> 00:23:41.980
I'm not really sure how
I got home after that.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
Next Time

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
Miracle
